Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Infra Topology", "GuideTitle",
 CellID->942062912,ExpressionUUID->"a3a3c038-ca24-47b7-9945-83f1c1312fe3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The topology of a substrate is read off its metric balls. The closed balls \
of one radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "122ead9d-4479-4673-bc64-d3d42a38e9cf"],
 " generate a topology: a vertex ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35f14924-a0ba-435b-a0da-b466700cd875"],
 " lies in the closure of a vertex ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ae327c10-f45a-4926-9ae9-2803678e1d04"],
 " when the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f6e7578f-4c8e-45bf-91af-5d03bde12ead"],
 "-ball at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "86d57c9c-e65e-43c7-8b07-bc2d11bd11f3"],
 " is contained in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6c2afa8d-bc2f-476b-8de3-50cdf316f50d"],
 "-ball at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c635c2d-2070-47d2-8ca4-c0da31db4a88"],
 ". This specialization preorder carries closure, interior, boundary, \
neighbourhood and continuity. A family of balls forms a complex through its \
intersections: a simplex is admitted when every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0d9b1015-2e91-4bfd-8aa9-dbc894fe5213"],
 " of its balls have a common point, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], "=", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d1d206d1-e301-4895-965d-48b68f15c6e1"],
 " gives the Vietoris-Rips complex of twice the radius, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], "=", "\[Infinity]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f8e8e86-4c7f-454e-a50a-710ee6e6a0bd"],
 " the Cech complex, and the orders between interpolate. The least number ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["N", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b88b84c4-8613-44ba-ba56-3c14fdf404a8"],
 " of balls of radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8686bfaa-9eb6-43af-acc9-adeceffe3dc7"],
 " that cover the substrate falls as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "44552ee5-ce30-4241-a9fd-98deedac09ff"],
 " grows, and the rate of that fall is a dimension."
}], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"]
}, Open  ]],

